From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilMetaMonkey <hood.mj85@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:17:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/31] Use captured Muse Code payloads; close only the named
 turn

Replace the synthetic Muse fixtures with scrubbed captures from Muse
Code 1.4.13 on macOS (exec run, unreachable-endpoint StopFailure, and an
interactive Esc for Interrupt).

Muse runs Interrupt handlers async, so a late Interrupt could arrive
after the next UserPromptSubmit and close the new turn's checkpoint.
Close events that carry a turn ID now close only a checkpoint with the
same turn; UserPromptSubmit still closes any turn left open in its
session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
